@missingId = 4b8d2f16-5c73-4a90-b1e2-8f3c6d05a721
@signature = data:image/png;base64,iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAAAEAAAABCAYAAAAfFcSJAAAADUlEQVR42mNk+M9QDwADhgGAWjR9awAAAABJRU5ErkJggg==AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAA

### =====================================================================
### 15. PROJECT LEDGER, LEGAL CLOSURE & IMMUTABILITY VAULT (FR-FIN, FR-CLS)
### =====================================================================
### The last mile: what a project cost, whether it made money, and the ceremony that turns its
### work records into a legal document nobody can change afterwards.
###
### The ledger splits VAT because VAT behaves in two ways — reclaimable input VAT passes through
### the company, non-deductible VAT is a real cost — and splits labour because a salaried
### technician's day is overhead the company pays regardless while a subcontractor's day is a
### cheque written for this job (FR-FIN-03). An expense that takes cumulative spend past the
### tenant's ceiling is held for management clearance: held, not hidden, because the money was
### already spent (FR-FIN-05).
###
### Closure is gated three ways — every field task signed off, a punch list that exists and has no
### open or failed line, and no expense still awaiting clearance — then dual-signed, client first
### and company second, then sealed. Sealing stamps the final margin, compiles the master archive,
### converts project-funded equipment to company assets (FR-FIN-04), and sets a write-lock enforced
### by a SaveChanges interceptor rather than by handler checks, so it holds for tables that do not
### exist yet.
###
### The full lifecycle — ledger arithmetic, the ceiling, both signatures in the wrong and right
### order, sealing, and the write-lock proven against seven distinct entity types — is covered by
### ClosureAndVaultLifecycleTests and ProjectMarginTests (xUnit) plus a 53-check scripted live run
### that drives one job from intake to a sealed record. This suite is a smoke test of the surface
### with explicit assertions. Field casing is camelCase (D-8).

### 15.1 Company Admin login
# @name companyAdminLogin
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: en

{ "email": "{{companyAdminEmail}}", "password": "{{companyAdminPassword}}" }

?? status == 200

@companyAdminToken = {{companyAdminLogin.data.token}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### The cost ledger (FR-FIN-02/03/06)
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### 15.2 The ledger for a job that does not exist -> 404
GET {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/workflow-instances/{{missingId}}/ledger
Authorization: Bearer {{companyAdminToken}}
Accept-Language: en

?? status == 404

### 15.3 A malformed ZATCA VAT number -> 400
### A registration number is exactly 15 digits. Accepting a malformed one produces a tax return
### the authority rejects, long after anyone remembers this invoice.
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/workflow-instances/{{missingId}}/ledger/expenses
Authorization: Bearer {{companyAdminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: en

{
  "vendorName": "Al-Faisal Supplies",
  "vendorTaxNumber": "12345",
  "invoiceReferenceNumber": "INV-1001",
  "description": "Smoke detectors",
  "subtotalAmount": 2000,
  "vatAmount": 300
}

?? status == 400

### 15.4 VAT larger than the goods -> 400
### Arithmetically possible only as a data-entry error, almost always the gross total typed into
### the VAT box.
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/workflow-instances/{{missingId}}/ledger/expenses
Authorization: Bearer {{companyAdminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: en

{
  "vendorName": "Al-Faisal Supplies",
  "vendorTaxNumber": "300012345600003",
  "invoiceReferenceNumber": "INV-1001",
  "description": "Smoke detectors",
  "subtotalAmount": 2000,
  "vatAmount": 3000
}

?? status == 400

### 15.5 An expense with no base amount -> 400
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/workflow-instances/{{missingId}}/ledger/expenses
Authorization: Bearer {{companyAdminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: en

{
  "vendorName": "Al-Faisal Supplies",
  "invoiceReferenceNumber": "INV-1002",
  "description": "Smoke detectors",
  "subtotalAmount": 0,
  "vatAmount": 0
}

?? status == 400

### 15.6 A well-formed expense on a job that does not exist -> 404
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/workflow-instances/{{missingId}}/ledger/expenses
Authorization: Bearer {{companyAdminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: en

{
  "vendorName": "Al-Faisal Supplies",
  "vendorTaxNumber": "300012345600003",
  "invoiceReferenceNumber": "INV-1003",
  "description": "Smoke detectors",
  "subtotalAmount": 2000,
  "vatAmount": 300,
  "isVatDeductible": true
}

?? status == 404

### 15.7 Booking zero time -> 400
POST {{HostAddress}}/api/v1/workflow-instances/{{missingId}}/ledger/labor
Authorization: Bearer {{companyAdminToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: en

{ "fieldWorkerId": "{{missingId}}", "units": 0, "workedOnUtc": "2026-09-20T08:00:00Z" }

?? status == 400

